<title>SPAIN: Beet sugar content at 17.2 pct in southern Spain.</title>
<headline>Beet sugar content at 17.2 pct in southern Spain.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average sugar content of beet in southern Spain tested at 17.2 percent at the factory gate on July 27, the National Sugar Beet association told Reuters on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Sugar content was at 17.24 percent on July 20 and at 17.33 percent on July 13.</p>
<p>To date, the southern harvest has yielded a crop of 1.43 million tonnes at an average sugar content of 17.2 percent, the association said.</p>
<p>The southern harvest continues into early August, while the northern harvest begins at the end of September or the start of October.</p>
<p>--Sharman Esarey, Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
